From 317bb739b4b57b265116e7c032a8152419dd5841 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:12:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 111/126] render: a particle sprite stands as in WE, its
 texture's first row at the top
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WE expands a sprite in the system's space (common_particles.h ComputeParticlePosition: v = 0 at
+up, `up` from the sprite's rotation and g_OrientationUp, GH 0x14024fd30), so a texture's first row is
at the sprite's top. LWE's particle space is WE's with y flipped (M_lwe = Fy·M_we·Fy), so WE's up
goes across as Fy·up = (0,−1,0) for the identity — but the orientation kept LWE's old (0,1,0): every
sprite was drawn mirrored top to bottom, and a turned one tilted the other way. Round sprites hid it;
light shafts (light_shafts_6, bright at its first row) didn't: 3354740764's and 1726902114's shafts
were lit from below, tilted the wrong way and drifted to the lower right of the field, where WE (both
references) has them hanging from the top of the sky.

g_OrientationUp = Fy·up, as Right and Forward already were.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-we-ref.md 3354740764 (light shafts WE doesn't draw there), 1726902114, 2561227934
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vg3T4kWN88ooeafgoHLbfM
---
 src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CParticle.cpp | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CParticle.cpp b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CParticle.cpp
index db2d870..b2ed030 100644
--- a/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CParticle.cpp
+++ b/src/core/WallpaperEngine/Render/Objects/CParticle.cpp
@@ -2539,9 +2539,11 @@ void CParticle::updateOrientation () {
     //                perpendicular to F
     //   upright (1): U = world y (bit 0) or the system's `axis` in the world; R = view forward × U; F = R × U
     //   fixed (2):   F = `axis`, U = its in-plane up — as given (bit 0) or the system's own, in the world
-    // LWE's particle space is WE's with y flipped (M_lwe = Fy·M_we·Fy, `updateMatrices`), and its sprites take
-    // (1,0,0)/(0,1,0)/(0,0,1) for WE's identity: R and F go across with Fy, U with −Fy, so with no rotation every
-    // mode is the identity LWE always drew
+    // LWE's particle space is WE's with y flipped (M_lwe = Fy·M_we·Fy, `updateMatrices`): R, U and F all go across
+    // with Fy, so WE's identity is (1,0,0)/(0,−1,0)/(0,0,1) here. The sprite's v = 0 (the texture's first row) is at
+    // +U (common_particles.h ComputeParticlePosition), so it sits at the top on screen, as in WE, and a sprite's
+    // own z rotation turns the way WE's does. (LWE drew U = (0,1,0): every sprite upside down, its rotation
+    // mirrored — 3354740764's and 1726902114's light shafts lit from below, tilted the other way)
     if (m_particle.renderers.empty () || m_particle.renderers[0].name != "sprite") {
 	// the trail and rope renderers have parsers of their own (not read): LWE's identity, as before
 	m_orientationRight = glm::vec3 (1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f);
@@ -2592,7 +2594,7 @@ void CParticle::updateOrientation () {
     right = unit (right, glm::vec3 (1.0f, 0.0f, 0.0f));
 
     m_orientationRight = fy * right;
-    m_orientationUp = -(fy * up);
+    m_orientationUp = fy * up;
     m_orientationForward = fy * forward;
 }
 
